{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00352 - MONDO_5224",
  "verbalization": "Tioguanine appears to be linked to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation through a series of indirect pathways, all involving Mitoxantrone. The evidence suggests that Tioguanine is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia and Myeloid Leukemia, both of which are classified under broader categories that ultimately lead to Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation. This indicates a potential pathway where Tioguanine may influence the development or progression of myeloid leukemia through its interaction with Mitoxantrone, which is known to be a treatment for various forms of leukemia. The overlapping indications and the shared downstream effect on Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation suggest a possible mechanism involving the pharmacological interaction between Tioguanine and Mitoxantrone, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Tioguanine may have a role in the pathogenesis of this leukemia type, though further research is needed to confirm the specific mechanism.",
